+`make MENU=1` builds the badge-menu firmware; a plain `make` builds the factory watch boot test
+instead. The build writes `SDK/cpu/br35/tools/app.bin` (the application image) and
+`SDK/cpu/br35/tools/update.ufw` (the native USB-flashable image). Flash `app.bin`/`update.ufw` with
+the device in USB bootloader mode.
 
-![img](http://www.kdocs.?)
+> **⚠️ The native `update.ufw` is NOT usable as-is for the BLE update (OTA).** It carries the
+> SDK-native uboot, which **cannot** perform the CODE-partition rewrite the BLE OTA requires: on
+> apply, the image verifies and the device reboots, but never boots again (silent brick). Turning
+> this image into a BLE-OTA-ready one requires additional packaging that is **out of scope of this
+> repository**.
 
+**Full build guide, the toolchain, and the execution order of both the build and the firmware:**
+see **[docs/BUILD.md](docs/BUILD.md)**.
 
+### Chipkey
 
-### 在线壁纸使用gif
+Packaging an image with the correct key needs your unit's flash key at
+`SDK/cpu/br35/tools/download/watch/chipkey_<id>.bin`, selected with `BADGE_CHIPKEY=<id>` (e.g.
+`BADGE_CHIPKEY=9847 make MENU=1`). The key is device-specific and is **not** committed — provide your
+own. Without it the build still completes (keyless image).
 
