+     * Do NOT answer this with a Service
+     * Changed indication: doing so breaks the standard HID connection sequence. Android
+     * subscribes to Service Changed as part of its initial GATT setup (BEFORE finishing the
+     * HID: read Report Map -> read Protocol Mode -> enable the Report 0x0028 notifications). If
+     * we fire a Service Changed indication (affected handles 0x0001..0xFFFF) the instant it
+     * subscribes, Android invalidates the discovery it has in progress and restarts, and
+     * never reaches "Enable Notifications" -> pairs+bonds but the Report CCC 0x0028 is never
+     * written, so the cursor stays dead. Confirmed on the UART: att_write 0x0035 -> we send the
+     * indication -> then NO 0x0027/0x002b reads AND no 0x0028 subscription.
+     *
+     * Service Changed only serves to invalidate a cache when an ALREADY-PAIRED device
+     * RECONNECTS and the DB changed since then. On a reconnect the CCC is restored from the bond
+     * WITHOUT a write, so this callback firing on 0x0035 always means a NEW subscription (initial
+     * setup) — exactly when the indication must NOT be sent. The stale-cache-after-reflash case
